From da27866f1ac5cec7ef521b558f061266162bca66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Oursland <jacob.oursland@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 18:20:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 147/197] Gui: Fix property-editor UAF from combo-box popup
 destroyed by rebuild

An enum property is edited with a QComboBox whose drop-down auto-opens on
FocusIn (PropertyItemDelegate). The drop-down is a top-level popup window Qt
registers in its active-popup list. When the property editor rebuilds
(PropertyModel::buildUp model reset, or row removal) it destroys the persistent
combo-box editor while the popup is still open, freeing the popup without Qt's
normal closePopup() teardown. A queued window-system mouse event is then
delivered to the freed popup and routed back into QComboBoxPrivate::itemSelected
on the dangling combo box, crashing with EXC_BAD_ACCESS (doActivate sender=0x400).

Close the popup in releaseEditorFocus() while the combo box is still alive so Qt
deregisters it and releases the mouse grab before the widget is freed. All
full-reset and row-removal paths already route through releaseEditorFocus().

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (claude-opus-4-8)
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5)
---
 src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp b/src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp
index 1600aef80..e2d0bbf67 100644
--- a/src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp
+++ b/src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include <boost/algorithm/string/predicate.hpp>
 #include <QApplication>
 #include <QClipboard>
+#include <QComboBox>
 #include <QCompleter>
 #include <QInputDialog>
 #include <QHeaderView>
@@ -477,6 +478,15 @@ void PropertyEditor::releaseEditorFocus()
     if (!activeEditor) {
         return;
     }
+
+    // An enum property is edited with a QComboBox whose drop-down is auto-opened by
+    // PropertyItemDelegate. Destroying the combo with the popup still open skips Qt's
+    // closePopup() teardown and leaves queued mouse events aimed at the freed popup,
+    // so close it while the combo is alive.
+    if (auto* combo = qobject_cast<QComboBox*>(activeEditor.data())) {
+        combo->hidePopup();
+    }
+
     for (QWidget* w = qApp->focusWidget(); w; w = w->parentWidget()) {
         if (w == activeEditor) {
             // setFocus() delivers a synchronous FocusOut that would otherwise cascade
